WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:06.960
It was July of 2004, and Bill Murray was enjoying
the peak of an extremely successful career.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:11.920
Not only had the iconic actor starred in some
of the most beloved comedies of the 20th Century,

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.820
including Ghostbusters and Groundhog Day,
he’d voiced the main character of the recently-released

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:18.800
live action Garfield movie.

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:22.490
It’d been a financial success, but it was
a critical flop.

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:28.449
Not that this bothered Bill – he was happy
with the performance... and the paycheck.

00:00:28.449 --> 00:00:32.480
What he wouldn’t be quite as happy about
was the horrifying encounter he was about

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.670
to have with SCP – 3166.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:42.089
On July 8th, Bill was enjoying a cold drink
on the porch of his luxurious Beverly Hills

00:00:42.089 --> 00:00:43.089
home.

00:00:43.089 --> 00:00:45.920
The sky was beginning to darken as the sun
set in the west.

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:47.969
It was a blissful evening.

00:00:47.969 --> 00:00:50.969
His wife, Jennifer, was inside, watching TV.

00:00:50.969 --> 00:00:56.179
Nothing seemed particularly out of the ordinary,
until he noticed a quick flash of orange in

00:00:56.179 --> 00:00:57.179
the distance.

00:00:57.179 --> 00:01:02.100
It was almost too fast to register, this large,
orange shape darting past the corner of his

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.100
eye.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:06.280
For a second, he entertained the thought that
it might have been an escaped tiger, but it

00:01:06.280 --> 00:01:08.690
was gone too fast to really tell.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.820
Bill finished his drink and headed inside.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:13.110
He’d had enough for one night.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:17.330
The next morning, he got up to read the paper,
and found the Garfield movie getting slaughtered

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.550
by the critics.

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:23.431
One review stated “no one can accuse Garfield:
The Movie of infidelity to its source: It

00:01:23.431 --> 00:01:28.640
faithfully conveys the banality of Jim Davis's
cartoon” Another called it“a film without

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:30.140
energy and without spirit.”

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:33.340
He put the paper down and ate his breakfast.

00:01:33.340 --> 00:01:38.920
A few blows to the ego were worth it for the
paydays that came with big budget family films.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:43.370
Just then his wife came to him with a strange
question: Were you walking around downstairs

00:01:43.370 --> 00:01:44.690
in the middle of the night?

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:48.270
No, he hadn’t, he’d been sleeping like
a baby.

00:01:48.270 --> 00:01:49.410
Why did she ask?

00:01:49.410 --> 00:01:50.410
“Well…”

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.410
Jennifer said.

00:01:51.410 --> 00:01:53.880
“I heard some rustling downstairs last night.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:56.020
It sounded like something big.”

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.409
He hadn’t heard anything though and told
her it was probably just her imagination.

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:03.300
He put it out of his mind and continued about
his day.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.060
He decided he would keep his eyes peeled for
that orange blur again though.

00:02:07.060 --> 00:02:12.040
Bill didn’t see anything peculiar the rest
of the morning and went to a local café for

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.040
lunch.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:16.829
He ordered a coffee and a cream cheese bagel,
then made a quick trip to the bathroom while

00:02:16.829 --> 00:02:18.379
his food was prepared.

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:22.590
When Bill returned to his table though, he
was something strange.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:26.739
Instead of a bagel, there was a large heaping
of lasagna on the table.

00:02:26.739 --> 00:02:28.060
What was going on?

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:30.569
This café didn’t even serve lasagna.

00:02:30.569 --> 00:02:34.069
Bill knew something was terribly wrong.

00:02:34.069 --> 00:02:38.790
Things only got stranger when Bill came home
to find a small tuft of orange fur snagged

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:40.380
on the frame of his front door.

00:02:40.380 --> 00:02:45.219
And it wasn’t synthetic fur like you see
on plush toys or stuffed animals.

00:02:45.219 --> 00:02:48.909
No, this was real animal fur.

00:02:48.909 --> 00:02:53.900
Maybe someone was just goofing off or trying
to play some weird prank on him, but it didn’t

00:02:53.900 --> 00:02:54.900
feel like it.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:59.239
Deep down, Bill Murray knew that he was in
grave danger.

00:02:59.239 --> 00:03:05.340
Whoever, or whatever, was behind this… it
wanted to hurt him.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:07.680
That night, his worst fears were realized.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.480
Bill’s wife had left town for the week and
he was heading to the kitchen in the middle

00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:16.290
of the night for a glass of water, when he
saw something - A huge figure moving up against

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:18.870
the glass door leading to his backyard.

00:03:18.870 --> 00:03:24.939
The thing was huge, nearly seven feet tall,
with a bloated, fur-covered, misshapen body

00:03:24.939 --> 00:03:27.739
that was pressed up against the door.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:32.930
Its fur was bright, garish orange – a cartoon
orange.

00:03:32.930 --> 00:03:36.290
Strangest of all though was the sound it was
making.

00:03:36.290 --> 00:03:38.950
It sounded like it was purring.

00:03:38.950 --> 00:03:42.750
Bill backed away from the door and then ran
back to his room to hide.

00:03:42.750 --> 00:03:47.469
The whole night, he sat cowering as he heard
scratching against the walls, like something

00:03:47.469 --> 00:03:49.079
was trying to get in.

00:03:49.079 --> 00:03:52.889
He was terrified and too scared to do anything,
even move.

00:03:52.889 --> 00:03:56.730
Finally, as morning broke, the noises seemed
to stop.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:58.189
Bill had to do something.

00:03:58.189 --> 00:04:00.120
He couldn’t let this nightmare go on another
night.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:02.420
What if things got worse?

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:05.760
What if that thing managed to get inside?

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:10.370
He called the local police and when they arrived,
he explained the incredibly strange situation

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:11.480
as best he could.

00:04:11.480 --> 00:04:16.250
He told them he was being stalked by some
kind of huge cat, or at least someone dressed

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.890
like a huge cat.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.810
Also there was lasagna involved.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:23.380
The officers interviewing him could barely
contain their laughter as he told them his

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:24.380
story.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:25.600
A giant orange cat?

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:30.440
Perhaps, one of them theorized, he’d angered
some kind of obsessive Garfield fan through

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:33.290
his involvement in the live action movie.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:38.430
After all, the original comic had been running
for years and had been extremely popular.

00:04:38.430 --> 00:04:43.050
Who knows what kind of nut jobs were obsessed
with seeing only a faithful adaptation of

00:04:43.050 --> 00:04:44.770
the source material?

00:04:44.770 --> 00:04:49.350
As the officers departed, Bill was confident
that they weren’t taking him seriously.

00:04:49.350 --> 00:04:51.720
He couldn’t rely on any of them for protection.

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:56.850
Thankfully, from a multi-decade movie career,
he had plenty of disposable income, and decided

00:04:56.850 --> 00:05:01.510
to hire a private security team to protect
him while he looked into this mystery.

00:05:01.510 --> 00:05:05.880
He had two trained bodyguards positioned around
his home at all times for the next month.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:10.540
They were armed, and given the cryptic orders
to fire on anything orange.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:14.110
Meanwhile, Bill began to fall down a Garfield
rabbit hole.

00:05:14.110 --> 00:05:19.200
He felt strangely compelled to research all
the Garfield media he could find, as though

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:24.020
the answer to his terrifying situation was
somehow hidden between the lines.

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:27.510
Bill explored the entire backlog of thousands
of comic strips.

00:05:27.510 --> 00:05:30.550
He read the books and interviews with Jim
Davis.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:34.170
He watched the cartoons and straight-to-DVD
animated movies.

00:05:34.170 --> 00:05:38.900
Ironically for a guy who’d recently portrayed
the lasagna-loving orange cat, Bill had never

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:42.620
felt quite so immersed in the character before.

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:48.120
He found a strange pathos in the routine of
Garfield and his friends.One particular comic

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.800
really piqued his interest, though.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.490
Originally published in October of 1989, the
comic began with Garfield being woken up by

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:58.640
a strange chill, an almost eerie sensation.

00:05:58.640 --> 00:06:02.380
The character observed aloud that he didn’t
feel like he was in his own home.

00:06:02.380 --> 00:06:06.590
He explored his little home further, trying
to find his owner Jon or his housemate and

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:10.830
sometimes nemesis, Odie, but found nothing.

00:06:10.830 --> 00:06:15.740
As Garfield remarked on feeling alone, a purple
speech box delivered the sinister message:

00:06:15.740 --> 00:06:21.759
“You have no idea how alone you are, Garfield.”

00:06:21.759 --> 00:06:25.840
He then finds that his home looks like it’s
been abandoned for years.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:29.700
The “For Sale” sign outside is practically
ancient.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:36.430
Garfield slowly comes to a horrifying revelation:
Everyone really is gone, and his adventures

00:06:36.430 --> 00:06:38.950
and friends now exist only in his imagination.

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:44.750
He’s trapped in a prison of his own creation,
trying to stave off his endless loneliness,

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:47.390
in denial about the reality of his situation.

00:06:47.390 --> 00:06:52.400
The comic ended with a quote directly from
Jim Davis himself, saying “An imagination

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.280
is a powerful tool.

00:06:54.280 --> 00:06:59.900
It can tint memories of the past, shade perceptions
of the present, or paint a future so vivid

00:06:59.900 --> 00:07:06.580
that it can entice... or terrify, all depending
upon how we conduct ourselves today...”

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:10.710
As he read those words, Bill Murray felt a
chill down his spine.

00:07:10.710 --> 00:07:14.420
Why had he wanted to get involved in the Garfield
movie in the first place?

00:07:14.420 --> 00:07:16.210
What had he gotten himself into?

00:07:16.210 --> 00:07:23.060
Before he could slip any deeper into his own
mind, Bill heard a faint, choked scream downstairs.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:25.050
He felt his breath catch in his throat.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:28.730
He was terrified but he needed to see what
was happening.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:32.720
He carefully and quietly began to creep down
the stairs.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:36.250
At the bottom, he poked his head around a
corner, and that’s when he saw a member

00:07:36.250 --> 00:07:39.150
of his security detail lying dead on the floor.

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:44.130
His face was blue from asphyxiation, his mouth
was stuffed with lasagna.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.420
It looked like he had been force-fed to death.

00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:52.560
Bill wanted to scream but he couldn’t, or
maybe knew he shouldn’t.

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:56.890
Just then he heard a soft, meaty thumping
noise coming from the nearby living room.

00:07:56.890 --> 00:08:02.940
He didn’t know why, but he felt compelled
to approach as if by forces beyond his control.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:08.910
He made his way to the living room, and when
he got there, he saw where the noise was coming

00:08:08.910 --> 00:08:09.910
from.

00:08:09.910 --> 00:08:12.310
Bill’s jaw dropped in pure horror.

00:08:12.310 --> 00:08:17.050
There was the other member of his security
detail, lying limp and lifeless under a giant

00:08:17.050 --> 00:08:18.050
orange figure.

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:23.050
It was a grotesquely huge creature, wearing
what looked to be a kind of crude Garfield

00:08:23.050 --> 00:08:25.930
outfit made of sewn-together cat pelts.

00:08:25.930 --> 00:08:28.520
It stank of pasta and rotten meat.

00:08:28.520 --> 00:08:34.450
In its giant paw, it held a golden trophy,
which it was using to pound the security guard’s

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:39.260
head into mush while making quiet, cat-like
purring noises.

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:44.010
The creature suddenly stopped and looked up,
locking eyes with Bill.

00:08:44.010 --> 00:08:46.240
The fear of death came over him.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:52.010
He froze, as the giant, freakish Garfield
stepped over Donny’s corpse, and began to

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:53.320
come towards him.

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:56.180
Bill turned and ran, but Garfield was gaining
on him.

00:08:56.180 --> 00:08:59.570
Before he could make it to the front door,
the creature knocked him over.

00:08:59.570 --> 00:09:04.010
He was laid out on the ground, looking up
at it, as it reached into its own body cavity

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:06.940
and began to pull out handfuls of lasagna.

00:09:06.940 --> 00:09:11.520
He was just about to shove a wad of the horrible
decaying pasta into Bill’s mouth, when suddenly,

00:09:11.520 --> 00:09:14.130
a DING was heard and the creature stopped.

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:19.740
It looked up, as if sniffing the air, and
then suddenly turned and lumbered towards

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:22.020
the kitchen.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:26.820
Bill watched as the Garfield monster entered
the kitchen where, somehow, there was a steaming

00:09:26.820 --> 00:09:30.020
hot fresh lasagna sitting in the open oven.

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:34.670
The creature had sensed the presence of external
lasagna, and felt the compulsion to integrate

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:40.060
it into its body, grabbing fistfulls and shoving
it into itself.

00:09:40.060 --> 00:09:44.630
Just then, a group of highly trained SCP Foundation
personnel burst into the room and subdued

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:46.180
the creature.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:47.790
It had been an ambush.

00:09:47.790 --> 00:09:51.060
The Foundation had been tipped off to the
presence of the creature by monitoring the

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:55.560
local police department dispatches, and the
report of a seven foot tall comic book cat

00:09:55.560 --> 00:09:59.710
terrorizing a Hollywood actor was definitely
worth looking into.

00:09:59.710 --> 00:10:06.170
The monster that had almost taken Bill Murray’s
life was SCP – 3166, a deadly pataphysical

00:10:06.170 --> 00:10:11.240
being that tends to manifest around people
somehow involved in the Garfield intellectual

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:12.240
property.

00:10:12.240 --> 00:10:16.060
It appears whenever the public perception
of Garfield falls out of favor, and because

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:20.570
Bill had starred in the critically-panned
Garfield movie, he was currently at the very

00:10:20.570 --> 00:10:24.650
top of SCP – 3166’s hit list.

00:10:24.650 --> 00:10:29.670
Thankfully, he managed to survive his terrifying
ordeal, and was administered amnestics by

00:10:29.670 --> 00:10:33.560
Foundation personnel so he could return to
his normal life.

00:10:33.560 --> 00:10:38.310
This frightening and mysterious creature has
been around since 1989, appearing after the

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:43.610
publication of the haunting Garfield comic
that Bill had read that very night.

00:10:43.610 --> 00:10:47.510
It appeared in the office of United Media,
who were the publishers of the Garfield comic

00:10:47.510 --> 00:10:51.010
strip at the time, and began wreaking havoc.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:55.520
Since then, the creature’s manifestation
has been a constant threat whenever Garfield

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:58.030
loses its popularity or audience.

00:10:58.030 --> 00:11:02.500
As a result, the Foundation has spent years
as the funding source behind all Garfield

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:06.940
media, and even planting hypnotic memetics
into the comic strips to ensure that there

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:09.870
is always a loyal fanbase.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:16.440
The fur is indeed real, organic cat fur, albeit
an unnaturally orange color, and instead of

00:11:16.440 --> 00:11:20.120
organs, the creature is filled with lasagna.

00:11:20.120 --> 00:11:24.660
Worst of all though, is that testing has revealed
that the meat in the lasagna is genetically

00:11:24.660 --> 00:11:29.350
identical to the flesh of Garfield’s creator,
Jim Davis.

00:11:29.350 --> 00:11:31.810
How did this thing come into existence?

00:11:31.810 --> 00:11:36.210
Perhaps it was Jim’s sheer force of imagination
that dragged it into being.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:41.270
As he himself said, “An imagination is a
powerful tool.”

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:44.880
All in all, it’s lucky that Bill Murray
was able to survive his encounter, and return

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:49.250
to his normal life – well, as normal as
life can be for Bill Murray.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:55.330
And if you see Bill Murray, don’t bother
asking him about SCP – 3166.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:12:01.020
The amnestics were quite effective, and just
as he’s fond of saying himself, no one will

00:12:01.020 --> 00:12:02.250
ever believe you.

00:12:02.250 --> 00:12:08.839
Now go check out “SCP – 5000 – The Suit”
and “SCP – 049 – The Plague Doctor Escapes”

00:12:08.839 --> 00:12:12.759
for more freaky and fascinating files from
your favourite Foundation!

